# Neo Sampler parameters (docs/specs/machines.md §5, Neo Sampler). The order is permanent: songs and presets
# store values by position. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoSampler
namespace NeoBuzz.Sampler
class NeoSamplerMachine
tracks 16
summary Sampler that plays the song's waves (wavetable slots, from wave_import) and built-in samples: 16 zones by key and velocity range, each with its wave, root, tune, level, pan, start, end, loop with crossfade, gate or one-shot, reverse and a choke group; a wave slot's layers split its keys by root or alternate round robin; amp and filter envelopes, velocity to level and filter, pitch bend; Kit mode puts zone n on key Kit base + n − 1 as a one-shot drum. Use it for drum kits, sampled instruments and one-shots.

group Play
Mode        "Mode"          0 1    0    enum Instrument Kit             | Instrument: each zone plays the notes in its key and velocity ranges, tuned from its root; Kit: zone n plays key Kit base + n − 1 at its own pitch, one-shot (key and velocity ranges, root, loop and trigger aside)
KitBase     "Kit base"      0 112  36   int 0 note                      | The key zone 1 plays in Kit mode (36 = C2, General MIDI's kick: zone 3 is D2 the snare, 7 F#2 the closed hat, 11 A#2 the open hat); the others follow a semitone apart
Polyphony   "Polyphony"     1 32   32   int 0 voices                    | Voices that sound at once (each zone a note plays takes one); past it a new voice takes the quietest released one, else the oldest, fading it out in 3 ms
BendRange   "Bend range"    0 24   2    int 0 st                        | Pitch bend range
VelAmp      "Vel → amp"     0 1000 700  pct                             | How much velocity sets the level: the gain is velocity^(2 × this) (100 %: velocity 64 is −12 dB; 0 %: every note at full level)
VelXfade    "Vel crossfade" 0 64   0    int 0 vel                       | Zones whose velocity ranges meet crossfade (equal power) over this many velocity steps around the boundary instead of switching; 0 switches
Volume      "Volume"        0 720  600  db -60 12 inf                   | Output level

group Amp env
AmpA        "Amp attack"    0 1000 0    time 0.0005 20                  | Attack time (the shortest, 0.5 ms, keeps a note starting mid-wave from clicking)
AmpD        "Amp decay"     0 1000 700  time 0.0005 20                  | Decay time (to −60 dB of the way to sustain)
AmpS        "Amp sustain"   0 1000 1000 pct                             | Sustain level
AmpR        "Amp release"   0 1000 538  time 0.0005 20                  | Release time after the note ends (to −60 dB)

group Filter
FType       "Filter"        0 4    0    enum Off LP_24 LP_12 BP HP      | Filter on every voice: off, ladder low-pass 24 or 12 dB/oct, state-variable band-pass or high-pass
FCutoff     "Cutoff"        0 1000 1000 freq 20 20000                   | Cutoff
FReso       "Resonance"     0 1000 0    pct                             | Resonance (the ladder self-oscillates at the top)
FEnv        "Filter env"    0 1000 500  bip                             | Filter envelope amount (±6 octaves)
FKey        "Key track"     0 1000 0    pct                             | Cutoff follows the keyboard around C4 (100 %: an octave per octave)
FVel        "Filter vel"    0 1000 0    pct                             | Softer notes close the filter (up to 3 octaves at the lowest velocity)

group Filter env
FltA        "Flt attack"    0 1000 0    time 0.0005 20                  | Attack time
FltD        "Flt decay"     0 1000 520  time 0.0005 20                  | Decay time
FltS        "Flt sustain"   0 1000 0    pct                             | Sustain level
FltR        "Flt release"   0 1000 538  time 0.0005 20                  | Release time

group Zone 1
Z1Wave    "Z1 wave"      0 254 1    int 0 wave            | Zone 1's wave: 0 off, 1–200 a slot of the song's wavetable (wave_import), 201 on a built-in sample (the manual lists them)
Z1KeyLo   "Z1 key low"   0 127 0    int 0 note             | Zone 1: the lowest key it plays (Instrument mode)
Z1KeyHi   "Z1 key high"  0 127 127  int 0 note             | Zone 1: the highest key it plays (Instrument mode)
Z1VelLo   "Z1 vel low"   1 127 1    int 0 vel              | Zone 1: the lowest velocity it plays (Instrument mode)
Z1VelHi   "Z1 vel high"  1 127 127  int 0 vel              | Zone 1: the highest velocity it plays (Instrument mode)
Z1Root    "Z1 root"      0 128 128  int 0 note             | Zone 1: the key that plays the wave unchanged; 128, Wave, takes each layer's own root from the wavetable (Instrument mode)
Z1Tune    "Z1 tune"      0 96  48   int -48 st signed      | Zone 1: transposition
Z1Fine    "Z1 fine"      0 2000 1000 lin -100 100 ct 1    | Zone 1: fine tune, in 0.1 cent steps
Z1Level   "Z1 level"     0 600 480  db -48 12 inf          | Zone 1: level
Z1Pan     "Z1 pan"       0 200 100  lin -100 100 % 0       | Zone 1: pan (a stereo wave: balance)
Z1Start   "Z1 start"     0 65534 0  lin 0 100 % 3          | Zone 1: where it starts, in % of the wave (the end, reversed)
Z1End     "Z1 end"       0 65534 65534 lin 0 100 % 3       | Zone 1: where it ends, in % of the wave (the start, reversed); it fades out over 2 ms before it
Z1Loop    "Z1 loop"      0 3   0    enum Wave Off Forward Ping-pong | Zone 1: Wave loops as the wavetable says (its loop points and type), Off plays through, Forward and Ping-pong loop between loop start and loop end
Z1LoopS   "Z1 loop start" 0 65534 0 lin 0 100 % 3          | Zone 1: loop start, in % of the wave (Forward, Ping-pong)
Z1LoopE   "Z1 loop end"  0 65534 65534 lin 0 100 % 3       | Zone 1: loop end, in % of the wave (Forward, Ping-pong)
Z1Xfade   "Z1 crossfade" 0 1000 215 pow 0 1 3 s 3          | Zone 1: a forward loop's crossfade (equal power), from the samples before loop start (after loop end, reversed); at most the loop's length and the room there is
Z1Trig    "Z1 trigger"   0 1   0    enum Gate One-shot     | Zone 1: Gate plays while the note is held, then releases; One-shot plays to the end and ignores note-offs and loops (Kit mode is one-shot)
Z1Rev     "Z1 reverse"   0 1   0    switch                 | Zone 1: plays backwards, from its end to its start
Z1Choke   "Z1 choke"     0 8   0    int 0                  | Zone 1: choke group 1–8 (0 off): a note in a group fades out, in 5 ms, every voice of the group still sounding (closed and open hats)

